{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-28-Oct-2022-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Let R be a point on a straight line PQ. Two Circles are drawn with diameters PR and PQ. Let A be any point on the circumference of the circle with diameter PQ. If PA meets the other circle at B, then:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "8,000", "added": false}, {"text": "7,400", "added": false}, {"text": "7,600", "added": false}, {"text": "7,800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "What is 20% of 45% of 800 grams?", "options": [{"text": "82 grams", "added": false}, {"text": "62 grams", "added": false}, {"text": "92 grams", "added": false}, {"text": "72 grams", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "A and B together completed a piece of work costing Rs. 1,900. A worked for 5 days, B for 6 days. If the daily wages of A and B are in the ratio of 4 : 3 respectively, then how much amount will be received by A?", "options": [{"text": "Rs. 800", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 900", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 1,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 1,100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "wages", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The distance between two parallel chords of length 10 cm, each in a circle of diameter 12 cm, is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A and B can accomplish a certain piece of work in 15 days when they work together. A alone can do that work in 30 days. If A and B work for 10 days and then onwards only A works. How long will it take for A to do the remaining task?", "options": [{"text": "25 days", "added": false}, {"text": "30 days", "added": false}, {"text": "20 days", "added": false}, {"text": "10 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "What is the volume of a hemisphere whose radius is 6 cm?", "options": [{"text": "451.16 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "454.16 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "453.16 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "452.57 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Aman's average score in a series of tests was ‘y’. He appeared in one more test and obtained score ‘z’. If Aman appeared in total ‘n’ tests, then which one of the following expression shows his average score for all the tests?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "A ship goes at a speed of 17 km/h downstream and at 13 km/h upstream. What will be the speed of the ship in still water?", "options": [{"text": "14 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "16 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "15 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "13 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "still-water-and-stream-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Sequences and Series", "sub": "arithmetic-progression", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The length and the breadth of a rectangular field are in the ratio 3 : 2. If the area of the field is 3456 m2, then what is the cost of fencing the field at the rate of Rs.3.50 per m?", "options": [{"text": "Rs. 240", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 840", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 480", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 420", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "In a government scheme, if an electricity bill is paid before due date, one gets a reduction of 13.5% on the amount of the bill. By paying the bill before due date, Ritu got a reduction of Rs. 6,075. The amount of her electricity bill was:", "options": [{"text": "Rs. 48,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 55,380", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 60,750", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs. 45,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "If interest is compounded half-yearly, then find the compound interest on ₹3,125 at 8% for 1 year.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "If x is a natural number such that 18 is the third proportional to (x + 2) and (x + 6), what is the value of x?", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "A man sells 10 pens for ₹18 gaining 24%. How many pens should he sell for ₹1,530 to earn a profit of 55%?", "options": [{"text": "540", "added": false}, {"text": "620", "added": false}, {"text": "680", "added": false}, {"text": "760", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "articles-and-batches", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "90° and 30°", "added": false}, {"text": "30° and 90°", "added": false}, {"text": "45° and 75°", "added": false}, {"text": "75° and 45°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}]}